From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: REPLACE-ME <you@example>
Date: Sat, 03 Oct 2026 03:55:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/dovi_rpudec: tag ICtCp frames from the RPU

Profile 5 codes its base layer in ICtCp, and signal_color_space is the only place in the
bitstream that says so. Nothing consumed it: a decoded P5 frame reached the filtergraph with
an unspecified colorspace, so any auto-inserted format or scale conversion applied a
Y'CbCr->RGB matrix to ICtCp samples and produced a picture that looked valid while being
wrong in direction.

Set AVCOL_SPC_ICTCP on the frame when the RPU declares ICtCp and the bitstream did not
contradict it. libswscale already refuses to colour-convert ICtCp (its decode/encode colour
helpers return ENOTSUP for it), so this converts a silent matrix misapplication into a
negotiation-time failure. A frame whose colorspace was explicitly signalled as something
else is logged and left alone rather than overridden.

Signed-off-by: REPLACE-ME <REPLACE-ME>
---
diff --git a/libavcodec/dovi_rpudec.c b/libavcodec/dovi_rpudec.c
index 79717f6..af61b5e 100644
--- a/libavcodec/dovi_rpudec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/dovi_rpudec.c
@@ -84,6 +84,22 @@ int ff_dovi_attach_side_data(DOVIContext *s, AVFrame *frame)
         return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
     }
 
+    /* The RPU is the only place that says what these planes actually hold: a Profile 5 base layer
+     * is coded in ICtCp (ITU-R BT.2100), while the container typically leaves matrix_coefficients
+     * unspecified. Left untagged, consumers assume Y'CbCr and libswscale will happily apply a
+     * BT.709/601 matrix to ICtCp samples; it refuses to convert a frame tagged AVCOL_SPC_ICTCP,
+     * so the tag is what turns that silent rematrisation into an explicit failure.
+     * An explicitly signalled different colorspace is left alone: RPU and bitstream disagreeing is
+     * a question to report, not a tie for a decoder to break. */
+    if (av_dovi_get_color(dovi)->signal_color_space == 2) {
+        if (frame->colorspace == AVCOL_SPC_UNSPECIFIED ||
+            frame->colorspace == AVCOL_SPC_ICTCP)
+            frame->colorspace = AVCOL_SPC_ICTCP;
+        else
+            av_log(NULL, AV_LOG_WARNING, "DOVI RPU signals ICtCp but the frame is tagged "
+                   "colorspace %d; leaving it alone\n", frame->colorspace);
+    }
+
     return 0;
 }
 
